      "AMANDA: OK, I should be out in about a half- hour. An hour if they work with me.\nMAX: Well-- Mom, can’t I come in?\nAMANDA: Max, honey, no. If you come in with me, it ages me ten years. Know what I mean? Here. Get a soda and wait for me in the car, OK?",
      "MAX: I’m gonna be in AP Calculus next year. And me and Vicki made the cheerleading squad, so I have to get a uniform and everything.\nAMANDA: That’s fantastic, honey, but... I don’t have the cash for that right now.\nMAX: Oh, you don’t have to-- it’s OK...\nAMANDA: OK, enough with the moping! Know what I mean? We’re gonna have fun! Who cares about those assholes anyway? We’re gonna party. Right?",
      "GERTIE: You do need help there, Max. Your GPA’s in rehab.\nMAX: Fine. Two semesters. And I’ll be there. But I won’t watch the movie. OK?",
      "VICKI: So what’s the story?\nGERTIE: Uh-- food gets caught in my braces after meals so I--\nVICKI: Not that. The movie tonight. Max. And don’t lie.",
      "VICKI: Oh, I feel so much better! What’s there to drink around here?\nMAX: There’s Drano under the sink.\nVICKI: I heard that, Max..."
    ]
  },
